---
// Privacy policy (D-002). Update the email-tool line once the tool is chosen.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TopBar from '../components/TopBar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { contactEmail } from '../data/site';

const updated = '17 November 2026';
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy policy | ShiftPatch"
	description="What ShiftPatch collects on this page, why, and how to have it deleted."
	noindex
>
	<TopBar />
	<main id="main" class="wrap policy">
		<h1>Privacy policy</h1>
		<p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

		<p>
			ShiftPatch is a pre-launch concept. Nothing has been built yet. This page exists to find
			out whether hospitals want it. This policy explains what we collect here, why, and how to
			get it deleted. If anything is unclear, email{' '}
			<a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>What we collect</h2>
		<h3>When you join the list</h3>
		<ul>
			<li>Your email address</li>
			<li>The role you pick (for example, nurse manager)</li>
			<li>
				Your answer to one optional question about how many short-notice shifts your facility
				fills in a month
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h3>When you visit the page</h3>
		<p>
			We use PostHog, an analytics tool, to see how people use this page: which pages are
			viewed, which buttons are clicked, whether the form is submitted, which version of the page
			you saw, and general details such as browser, device type and approximate location
			(country or city, worked out from your IP address).
		</p>
		<p>
			By default this runs <strong>without cookies</strong>, and we can't recognise you if you
			come back on a different day. If you accept cookies in the banner, PostHog also sets a
			cookie so we can tell repeat visits apart, and records your session (mouse movement,
			scrolling and clicks) so we can see where the page is confusing.
			<strong>Session recordings hide everything typed into form fields.</strong> If you
			decline, there are no cookies and no recordings.
		</p>

		<h3>Emails</h3>
		<p>
			We use an email service provider (named here once chosen) to send you three emails from{' '}
			{contactEmail}: a welcome and two follow-ups. It may tell us whether an email was opened
			or a link was clicked, and we pass those events to PostHog so we can see which messages
			are useful.
		</p>

		<h2>Why we collect it</h2>
		<p>
			Only to find out whether ShiftPatch is worth building, and to send you the three emails you
			signed up for. We don't sell your data, use it for advertising, or share it with anyone
			except the services named on this page.
		</p>

		<h2>Where it's stored</h2>
		<p>PostHog stores our analytics data in the United States.</p>

		<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
		<p>
			You can ask us to delete your data at any time. Either way, we delete everything within six
			months of the end of this test.
		</p>

		<h2>Your choices</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Decline cookies in the banner. The page works the same either way.</li>
			<li>Unsubscribe from any email using the link in it.</li>
			<li>
				Ask for a copy of your data, a correction, or deletion by emailing{' '}
				<a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. This applies wherever you are,
				including the EU and Brazil.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</main>
	<Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
	.policy {
		max-width: calc(var(--measure) + 2 * var(--gutter));
		padding-block: 2.5rem 3rem;
	}

	h1 {
		font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 2.6rem);
		margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
	}

	.updated {
		color: var(--ink-muted);
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	h2 {
		font-size: 1.45rem;
		margin-top: 2.25rem;
		padding-top: 1rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	h3 {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
	}

	ul {
		padding-left: 1.2rem;
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
	}

	li {
		margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
	}
</style>
